    summary: "新墨西哥州陪審團裁定 Meta（Facebook 母公司）欺騙用戶關於平台隱私保護，這標誌著對該科技巨頭的重大法律挫敗。陪審團裁定公司違反了超過 4300 萬項州消費者保護法規。此次訴訟的核心指控是 Meta 透過第三方性格測驗，收集了約 8700 萬個用戶的數據，並將其出售給政治顧問公司 Cambridge Analytica，用於生成定向廣告，這與 2016 年唐納德·川普的競選活動有關。陪審團認為 Meta 對保護用戶數據做出了誤導性陳述，影響了新墨西哥州超過兩百萬人口。儘管 Meta 辯稱州方的證據已過時，但陪審團仍判其有誤導公眾關於處理 Cambridge Analytica 醜聞後第三方應用程式開發者數據採集調查的行為。最終的罰款金額將由法官決定，但州方要求每項違規處以最高 $5,000 的罰款。",
    tags: ["Meta", "Facebook", "新墨西哥州", "Cambridge Analytica", "隱私保護", "消費者保護法規"],
    title_en: "New Mexico Jury Rules Meta Deceived Users on Privacy Protection, Citing Alleged Cambridge Analytica Data Misuse",
    summary_en: "A New Mexico jury ruled that Meta (Facebook's parent company) deceived users regarding platform privacy protection, marking a significant legal setback for the tech giant. The jury found the company violated over 43 million state consumer protection laws. The core allegation in the lawsuit was that Meta collected data from approximately 87 million users through third-party personality quizzes and sold it to political consulting firm Cambridge Analytica for targeted advertising, linked to Donald Trump's 2016 presidential campaign. The jury determined that Meta made misleading statements about protecting user data, affecting over two million people in New Mexico. Although Meta argued that the state's evidence was outdated, the jury still found it liable for misleading the public regarding its data collection practices from third-party application developers following the Cambridge Analytica scandal. The final penalty amount will be determined by the judge, but the state is seeking a fine of up to $5,000 for each violation.",
    tags_en: ["Meta", "Facebook", "New Mexico", "Cambridge Analytica", "Privacy Protection", "Consumer Protection Laws"],
