    summary_en: "Debian has released security advisory DSA-6525-1, which patches a potential security vulnerability discovered in the OpenSSH service. This vulnerability may affect systems running specific versions of the OpenSSH service. Although the original text does not provide detailed technical specifics or a CVSS score, such patches typically involve enhancing service security to prevent remote attackers from gaining unauthorized access or executing malicious code using unpatched services. All users running Debian systems and utilizing the OpenSSH service are advised to immediately update their systems to the latest version containing this security patch to ensure system integrity and security. Users should apply the patch through standard system update mechanisms (such as apt update/upgrade) to avoid potential security risks.",
    tags_en: ["Debian", "OpenSSH", "DSA-6525-1", "Linux Kernel", "Security Update"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Debian Security", url: "https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00438.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
