    id: "20260928-13284",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "AI行為者 JadePuffer 攻擊 Azure 租戶：透過洩露憑證進行大規模雲端破壞",
    summary: "Microsoft 報告了由追蹤代號 JadePuffer（亦被稱為 Storm-3168）的行為者發動的雲端攻擊。該攻擊者利用洩露的 Azure 服務主體憑證，在 Azure 租戶內進行了高度自動化的破壞行動，目標包括刪除儲存帳戶、應用程式和資料庫。攻擊流程首先進行了長時間的偵察（Reconnaissance），透過兩個服務主體，詳細繪製了受害者環境的虛擬機器、資源群組和訂閱範圍。隨後，攻擊者開始執行破壞操作，成功刪除了多個儲存帳戶、Azure Key Vault、Function App 和 App Service plan。Microsoft 指出，攻擊者最初的憑證（Client ID, Client Secret, Tenant ID）曾在受影響組織的 GitHub 公開 Issue 中以明文形式洩露。為防止類似事件，Microsoft 建議客戶啟用 Microsoft Defender for Cloud 等保護措施，並持續評估和保護應用程式憑證和密鑰，以應對 AI 協調的攻擊威脅。",
    tags: ["JadePuffer", "Azure", "服務主體", "雲端安全", "憑證洩露", "攻擊行動"],
    title_en: "AI Actor JadePuffer Attacks Azure Tenants: Large-Scale Cloud Destruction via Leaked Credentials",
    summary_en: "Microsoft reported a cloud attack launched by an actor tracked as JadePuffer (also known as Storm-3168). This attacker utilized leaked Azure Service Principal credentials to conduct highly automated destructive actions within an Azure tenant, targeting the deletion of storage accounts, applications, and databases. The attack process began with extensive reconnaissance, where the attacker used two service principals to map the victim's environment, including virtual machines, resource groups, and subscription scopes. Subsequently, the attacker executed destructive operations, successfully deleting multiple storage accounts, Azure Key Vaults, Function Apps, and App Service plans. Microsoft noted that the attacker's initial credentials (Client ID, Client Secret, Tenant ID) were leaked in plaintext within a public GitHub issue of the affected organization. To prevent similar incidents, Microsoft advises customers to enable protective measures like Microsoft Defender for Cloud and to continuously assess and protect application credentials and keys against AI-coordinated attack threats.",
    tags_en: ["JadePuffer", "Azure", "Service Principal", "Cloud Security", "Credential Leakage", "Attack"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Dark Reading", url: "https://darkreading.com/cloud-security/jadepuffer-ai-actor-azure-tenant-destructive-cloud-attack", lang: "EN" }
    ]
