    summary_en: "Anthropic announced an upgrade to its mid-sized AI model, Claude Sonnet, from Sonnet 5 to Sonnet 5.5. Sonnet 5.5 is positioned as the best performer for general daily tasks, excelling particularly in tasks such as error correction, creating polished documents, slides, and spreadsheets. Compared to Sonnet 5, Sonnet 5.5 is described as having clearer writing and faster speed, making it suitable for non-complex tasks requiring rapid iteration, and early testers have praised it as a better collaborative partner. In terms of performance, while Sonnet 5.5 retains the pricing of Sonnet 5, Anthropic points out that it consumes fewer tokens to complete the same work and generates output more than 30% faster than Sonnet 5, making it the fastest Sonnet model to date. Furthermore, Sonnet 5.5 introduces network security safeguards and fallbacks, similar to Anthropic's top-tier model, for the first time in the Sonnet series, bringing its cybersecurity capabilities on par with Opus 5. The biological safety mechanisms remain unchanged from Sonnet 5. This upgrade aims to enhance the practicality and security of the Sonnet series models, allowing for broader application in commercial and development workflows.",
