    title: "CISO調查：AI深造偽詐騙攻擊已成為常態，企業需強化多層防禦體系",
    summary: "根據Gartner針對297位CISO或同級高階主管的調查顯示，高階主管中已有41%在過去一年內曾遭遇利用Deepfake技術的語音詐騙（vishing）攻擊，而透過視訊通話的攻擊比例亦達36%。調查指出，AI技術提高了社會工程攻擊的頻率、個人化程度和說服力，但同時降低了傳統偵測跡象的可靠性。參與調查的CISO中，有79%曾遭遇電子郵件釣魚或魚叉式釣魚，58%則發生過vishing或smishing事件。為有效應對這種演進的AI驅動社會工程攻擊，Gartner建議CISO應採取三項核心措施：第一，將傳統教育轉為適應性安全行為與文化計畫，強調在接收高風險請求時必須執行安全確認流程；第二，強化員工身分與復原機制，對特權存取、帳號復原等關鍵流程實施防釣魚認證和風險基礎身分控制；第三，建立AI媒介威脅的偵測與應對體系，需將可疑聯絡、假冒通報資訊與帳號復原紀錄、新設備登入、權限變更等進行關聯分析，並更新事故應對手冊以應對多模態假冒和AI代理的濫用。",
    tags: ["CISO", "Deepfake", "社會工程攻擊", "vishing", "Gartner", "AI安全"],
    title_en: "CISO Survey: AI-Enhanced Deepfake Scams Are Now Routine, Requiring Enterprises to Strengthen Multi-Layered Defenses",
    summary_en: "According to a Gartner survey of 297 CISOs or equivalent senior executives, 41% of senior leaders reported encountering voice phishing (vishing) attacks utilizing Deepfake technology within the past year, with the proportion of attacks via video calls reaching 36%. The survey indicates that AI technology has increased the frequency, personalization, and persuasiveness of social engineering attacks, while simultaneously reducing the reliability of traditional detection indicators. Among the participating CISOs, 79% reported experiencing email phishing or spear-phishing, and 58% reported vishing or smishing incidents. To effectively counter these evolving AI-driven social engineering attacks, Gartner recommends that CISOs adopt three core measures: First, transition traditional education into adaptive security behavior and culture programs, emphasizing the mandatory execution of security verification processes when receiving high-risk requests. Second, strengthen employee identity and recovery mechanisms, implementing anti-phishing authentication and risk-based identity controls for critical processes such as privileged access and account recovery. Third, establish a detection and response system for AI-mediated threats, which requires correlating suspicious communications, impersonation notifications, account recovery records, new device logins, and permission changes, and updating incident response playbooks to address multi-modal impersonation and AI agent misuse.",
