    title_en: "KISA and Ministry of Science and ICT Host Academic Competition on 'Law in the Digital Age' to Explore Legal Issues in AI and Digital Transformation",
    summary_en: "The Korea Internet & Security Agency (KISA) and the Ministry of Science and ICT (MSIT) jointly hosted the '1st Law for Digital' academic competition. This event aims to identify new legal issues arising from the rapid development of AI and digital transformation, and to seek solutions. The competition topics covered various legal issues in the digital domain, including blockchain, spam, electronic signatures, electronic documents, location information, URLs, and digital dispute mediation. Participants included students from law professional universities nationwide, senior lawyers, and legal PhDs. The event emphasized the combination of academic research and practical policy formulation, aiming to transform innovative academic ideas into actual legal and systemic improvements. The Director of KISA stated that with the development of digital technology, proactively discussing and establishing reasonable legal system solutions is crucial, and that they will continue to expand opportunities for professional exchange.",
